This is the **Feit–Thompson conjecture on primes**, a well-known open problem in number theory. It states that for distinct primes $p < q$, the repunit-like quantity $\frac{q^p - 1}{q - 1}$ never divides $\frac{p^q - 1}{p - 1}$.

